<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <EntityComponents>

<!-- 2026-08-27: Port installations are static, invulnerable, uneditable buildings (see
     SpawnGroups-Ports.sbc)  - they don't patrol or produce anything, so unlike the Factory
     behaviors these only run the Store-sales trigger plus (2026-08-28) a defensive plane
     scramble, same pattern as the Factories'. See WW2-Store-Behavior-PortSales.sbc and
     Triggers-DefensiveSpawn-Port.sbc for the trigger/action pairs.

     2026-08-30: split from one shared Behavior per faction into one Behavior per port. Store
     sales and defensive scramble are still identical per faction (faction-only, no per-port
     logic), but each port now also runs its own Triggers-CargoSpawn-Port.sbc trigger, and La
     Spezia/Tripoli (and Oran/Toulon) each need a DIFFERENT one - a shared Behavior can't hold
     two different one-directional cargo routes. SpawnGroups-Ports.sbc <Behaviour> tags updated
     to match.

     2026-09-07: briefly removed the WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Port-Gray/Green trigger
     references below, on a wrong diagnosis that ApplyStoreProfiles itself was crashing the
     client on Store Block interact. Root cause actually confirmed via the real crash log
     (NullReferenceException in Sandbox.Game.Screens.ViewModels.MyMarketWatchViewModel, thrown
     the instant any Store Block UI opens) to be <EnableEconomy>false</EnableEconomy> in this
     world's Sandbox_config.sbc - not anything MES-side. Confirmed by reading GV Deserts of
     Kharak's own GVK-Derelicts mod (Workshop 2653133286): it uses this exact same
     ApplyStoreProfiles/RequiredOffers mechanism successfully on a fully custom, MES-heavy planet
     with Economy enabled. Triggers restored below to the original working pattern - see
     WW2-Store-Behavior-PortSales.sbc, unchanged. The real fix is enabling Economy properly on
     this world (both <EnableEconomy> in Sandbox_config.sbc AND <GenerateFactionsOnStart> in
     Sandbox.sbc's SessionComponentEconomy block are needed for an EXISTING save per the MES
     Economy-Stations-FAQ - Sandbox_config alone was tested and hung on load, untested with both
     flags set together).

     2026-09-10: each port now runs TWO Store-sales triggers instead of one - a shared
     WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods (identical everywhere, targets the "Store-Port-
     Goods" block) plus a faction-specific WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Gray/Green
     (targets the "Store-Port-Vehicles" block) - two separate physical Store blocks per
     location, kept deliberately independent per direct request rather than merged into one
     block/one profile. See WW2-Store-Behavior-PortSales.sbc for the full writeup. -->

<!-- Gray -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-Port-Gray-LaSpezia</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>
			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods]
			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Gray]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-DefenseSpawn-Port-Gray]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-CargoSpawn-Port-LaSpezia]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-Port-Gray-Tripoli</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>
			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods]
			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Gray]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-DefenseSpawn-Port-Gray]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-CargoSpawn-Port-Tripoli]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

<!-- Green -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-Port-Green-Oran</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>
			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods]
			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Green]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-DefenseSpawn-Port-Green]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-CargoSpawn-Port-Oran]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-Port-Green-Toulon</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>
			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods]
			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Green]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-DefenseSpawn-Port-Green]
			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-CargoSpawn-Port-Toulon]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

<!-- Valencia (neutral, TRADER faction) - deliberately NO reputation-damage trigger and NO
     defensive-scramble trigger, unlike every Gray/Green port above. This is what actually
     guarantees standing here can never go hostile (see Factions.sbc's own note) and keeps the
     post genuinely non-combative - it just sells. No cargo-spawn trigger either since Valencia
     doesn't run a cargo-ship route to another port. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-Port-Valencia</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>
			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-PortGoods]
			[Triggers:WW2-Store-Trigger-UpdateSales-Vehicles-Valencia]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

	</EntityComponents>
</Definitions>
